{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[G]mazing grace, how [G7]sweet the [C]sound
That [G]saved a wretch like [D]me
I [G]once was lost, but [G7]now am [C]found
Was [G]blind, but [D]now I [G]see
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
'Twas [G]grace that taught my [G7]heart to [C]fear
And [G]grace my fears re[D]lieved
How [G]precious did that [G7]grace ap[C]pear
The [G]hour I [D]first be[G]lieved
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Through [G]many dangers, [G7]toils and [C]snares
I [G]have already [D]come
'Tis [G]grace hath brought me [G7]safe thus [C]far
And [G]grace will [D]lead me [G]home
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
A[G]mazing grace, how [G7]sweet the [C]sound
That [G]saved a wretch like [D]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
The [G]Lord has promised [G7]good to [C]me
His [G]word my hope se[D]cures
He [G]will my shield and [G7]portion [C]be
As [G]long as [D]life en[G]dures
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Yea, [G]when this flesh and [G7]heart shall [C]fail
And [G]mortal life shall [D]cease
I [G]shall possess with[G7]in the [C]veil
A [G]life of [D]joy and [G]peace
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
The [G]earth shall soon dis[G7]solve like [C]snow
The [G]sun forbear to [D]shine
But [G]God, who called me [G7]here be[C]low
Will [G]be for[D]ever [G]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
When [G]we've been there ten [G7]thousand [C]years
Bright [G]shining as the [D]sun
We've [G]no less days to [G7]sing God's [C]praise
Than [G]when we [D]first be[G]gun
{end_of_verse}

